"[2601.10348] Training-Trajectory-Aware Token Selection (https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.10348)\nciteturn30920view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.10348\",\"lineno\":0}); Total lines: 163\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Computation and Language\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 15 Jan 2026 (cite5†v1 ), last revised 21 May 2026 (this version, v2)]\nL9: # Title:Training-Trajectory-Aware Token Selection\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite6†Zhanming Shen , cite7†Jiaqi Hu , cite8†Zeyu Qin , cite9†Hao Chen , cite10†Wentao Ye , cite11†Zenan Huang , cite12†Yihong Zhuang , cite13†Guoshan Lu , cite14†Junlin Zhou , cite15†Junbo Zhao L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Training-Trajectory-Aware Token Selection, by Zhanming Shen and 9 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite16†View PDF cite17†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:Efficient distillation is a key pathway for converting expensive reasoning capability into deployable efficiency, yet in the frontier regime where the student already has strong reasoning ability, naive continual distillation often yields limited gains or even degradation. We observe a characteristic training phenomenon: even as loss decreases monotonically, all performance metrics can drop sharply at almost the same bottleneck, before gradually recovering.\nL17: We further uncover a token-level mechanism: confidence bifurcates into steadily increasing Imitation-Anchor Tokens that quickly anchor optimization and other yet-to-learn tokens whose confidence is suppressed until after the bottleneck. And the characteristic that these two types of tokens cannot coexist is the root cause of the failure in continual distillation.\nL18: To this end, we propose Training-Trajectory-Aware Token Selection (T3S) to reconstruct the training objective at the token level, clearing the optimization path for yet-to-learn tokens. T3S yields consistent gains in both AR and dLLM settings: with only hundreds of examples, Qwen3-8B surpasses DeepSeek-R1 on competitive reasoning benchmarks, Qwen3-32B approaches Qwen3-235B, and T3-trained LLaDA-2.0-Mini exceeds its AR baseline, achieving state-of-the-art performance among all of 16B-scale no-think models.\nL19: Comments:  | Accepted by ICML 2026\nL20: Subjects:  | Computation and Language (cs.CL); Artificial Intelligence (cs.AI); Machine Learning (cs.LG)\nL21: Cite as:  | cite18†arXiv:2601.10348 [cs.CL]\nL22:    | (or cite19†arXiv:2601.10348v2 [cs.CL] for this version)\nL23:    | cite20†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2601.10348†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL24: ## Submission history\nL25: \nL26: From: ZhanMing Shen [cite21†view email ]\nL27: cite5†[v1] Thu, 15 Jan 2026 12:45:05 UTC (1,872 KB)\nL28: [v2] Thu, 21 May 2026 06:29:24 UTC (1,999 KB)\nL29: \nL30: Full-text links:\nL31: \nL32: ## Access Paper:\nL33: \nL34: View a PDF of the paper titled Training-Trajectory-Aware Token Selection, by Zhanming Shen and 9 other authors\nL35: \nL36:   * cite16†View PDF L37:   * cite17†HTML (experimental) L38:   * cite22†TeX Source L39: \nL40: cite23†view license†creativecommons.org L41: ### Current browse context:\nL42: \nL43: cs.CL\nL44: \nL45: cite24†< prev |   cite25†next > L46: \nL47: cite26†new | cite27†recent | cite28†2026-01 L48: \nL49: Change to browse by:\nL50: \nL51: cite29†cs L52: cite30†cs.AI L53: cite31†cs.LG L54: \nL55: ### References & Citations\nL56: \nL57:   * cite32†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L58:   * cite33†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L59:   * cite34†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L60: \nL61: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL62: \nL63: ## BibTeX formatted